---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About — health4.ai"
  description="What health4.ai is, who built it, and how it works: a free iOS app that moves Apple Health data to a Google Sheet or database you own, plus an open-source MCP server."
>
  <nav class="flex items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <a href="/" class="text-green-400 font-bold text-lg tracking-tight hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">health4.ai</a>
  </nav>

  <main class="px-6 py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-invert prose-sm">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-2">About health4.ai</h1>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">What it is</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        health4.ai is a free iOS app that moves Apple Health data to a destination you
        own: a Google Sheet in your own Google Drive (one row per day, the easiest option),
        or your own Postgres/Supabase database (every HealthKit sample, for power users).
        An open-source MCP (Model Context Protocol) server and in-app Connect Your AI
        config (database option) let Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and other MCP-compatible clients use that
        data. Background sync is best-effort, since iOS decides when the app runs, and
        the phone does not need to be on the same Wi-Fi network as the AI client.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">Why it exists</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Apple has no server-side HealthKit API, so most tools that connect health data to
        an AI either require the phone and the AI client to be on the same local network,
        or only work inside a single vendor's web app. health4.ai closes that gap by
        syncing HealthKit data to a Google Sheet or database the user controls, reachable from
        anywhere, so that standard MCP clients can work with it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">How data flows</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The iPhone app sends data directly to a Google Sheet in the user's own Drive
        (Google scope drive.file, so the app only sees files it creates), or to a Supabase
        project the user owns via a Supabase Edge Function. For the database option, the
        MCP server (FastMCP, Python) reads from that database and answers tool calls from
        Claude, Cursor, or any other MCP client. There is no health4.ai account and no
        health4.ai server, and health4.ai never receives, stores, or has access to a
        user's health data. See the{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a> for
        the full data-handling description.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">Open source</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Both the iOS app and the MCP server are open source under the MIT license on{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">GitHub</a>.
        Anyone can read the code, self-host the MCP server against their own Supabase
        project, or contribute.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-3">Who runs it</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        health4.ai is an independent, free software project. It is not affiliated with
        Apple, Anthropic, OpenAI, or Cursor; product names on this site are used only to
        describe compatibility. Questions go to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@health4.ai" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">hello@health4.ai</a>.
        health4.ai is not a medical device and does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent
        any disease or health condition — see the{' '}
        <a href="/terms/" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-neutral-800/60 px-6 py-8 mt-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-neutral-600 text-xs">
      <span>© 2026 health4.ai · Not a medical device</span>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
        <a href="/about/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">About</a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Contact</a>
        <a href="/privacy/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Terms</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
